# Changelog

All notable changes to linux-labs. The version matches `Version:` in rpm/linux-labs.spec and the git tag vX.Y.Z.

## Unreleased

### Added
- Lab samba-01 (Storage, Intermediate, two nodes): a Samba share for a group with samba_share_t and the samba firewall service, mounted persistently on node 2 through fstab with a credentials file.
- Lab ansible-02 (Automation, Intermediate, three nodes): an Ansible role with defaults, templates and a handler, variables in group_vars and host_vars, and a playbook that applies it.
- Lab files-05 (Files, Beginner): find files by owner, size, age and permissions, search a log with grep, and keep a command's errors apart from its output.
- Lab podman-02 (Containers, Intermediate): build an image from a Containerfile with a label and an environment variable, and run it rootless with a published port, a named volume and a restart policy.
- Lab users-04 (Users, Intermediate): a password policy with pwquality, account lockout with faillock and password history through authselect features.
- Lab time-01 (Networking, Intermediate, two nodes): node 1 serves time with chrony from a local stratum, and node 2 synchronises only from node 1 and uses the time zone Europe/Zagreb.
- Lab logging-04 (Logging, Intermediate): persistent audit rules in rules.d for a file watch and a deletion rule by login UID, and auditd log settings.
- Lab nfs-02 (Storage, Intermediate, two nodes): an all_squash export with a fixed anonymous user, a read-only export, and on-demand mounts through an autofs indirect map.
- Lab ansible-01 (Automation, Beginner, three nodes): an Ansible control node on servera with ansible.cfg, an inventory, key access to a sudo account on the managed nodes and a playbook that installs and starts httpd. Automation is a new category.
- Lab storage-04 (Storage, Intermediate, reboot): a persistent swap file with a priority, vm.swappiness in sysctl.d and a tuned profile.
- Lab ssh-02 (SSH, Advanced): sshd hardening with key-only root login, a Match block that disables passwords for a group, and a second port with its SELinux type and firewall rule.
- Lab podman-01 (Containers, Advanced): a rootless httpd container with an SELinux-labelled volume, run as a systemd user service with linger. Containers is a new category.
- Lab nfs-01 (Storage, Intermediate, two nodes): an NFS export from node 1 to node 2 only, with root squashing, and a persistent mount on node 2.
- Lab ssh-01 (SSH, Beginner): an ed25519 key pair, an authorized key for a second account and a client host alias. SSH is a new category.

## 2.0.0 (2026-10-03)

### Added
- Lab framework 2.0. Every lab now has seven files: setup.sh, task.txt, grade.sh, cleanup.sh, description.txt, solution.md and a repo-only solve.sh that never ships in the RPM.
- task.txt for each lab, which states the end state and never the solving commands. labctl start prints a standard header followed by the task.
- labctl task, to show the task of a lab again after it was started.
- lib/grading.sh, the shared grader library. Every grader prints the same PASS/FAIL criterion lines and a final result, replacing the per-lab pass/fail helpers.
- scripts/check-labs.sh, run in CI, which enforces the lab contract: required files, task text rules (with scripts/check-labs.allow for reviewed false positives), shellcheck, the allowed repository root files and an up-to-date catalog.
- scripts/test-lab.sh, which runs one lab at a time against a test host (start, solve, grade, reset), and scripts/solve-lib.sh for the solve.sh scripts.
- Lab systemd-04. The collection is now 55 labs in 17 topics.
- A needs: key in description.txt (internet, reboot, free-nic, nodes=N), cross-checked against the lab by check-labs.sh and shown in the task header.
- A generated lab catalog, docs/catalog.md, built by scripts/gen-catalog.sh. CI fails when it is stale.
- labctl --version, which prints the installed linux-labs version.
- labctl list --course and --level filters.
- Student documentation installed under /usr/share/doc/linux-labs.
- LICENSE file in the repository root.
- A new-lab project skill that builds labs from the idea list.
- Hints: an optional `## Hints` section in solution.md, shown one at a time by labctl hint <lab> (with --all for teachers). All 55 labs have hints, and check-labs.sh enforces 2 to 4 hints with no solving commands.
- labctl solution asks for confirmation in a terminal; --yes skips the question.
- A new GitHub Pages site: front page with the install command and an example labctl session, the lab catalog, and the student guides rendered from docs/student. scripts/preview-pages.sh builds and serves it locally.
- Per-lab known issues: an optional labs/<id>/known-issues.md that check-labs.sh validates and the catalog counts in a new "Known issues" column. It stays in the repo and is never shipped in the RPM.
- Release notes come from this file: scripts/release-notes.sh extracts the section of the tagged version, and the release fails when it is missing.
- Lab targets: a target: key in description.txt names the machine a single-node lab runs on. For a server target labctl sends the lab and lib/ to the server over SSH and runs setup, grade and cleanup there as root through opsadmin's passwordless sudo, with the output streamed to the student's terminal.
- The task header of a lab on a server ends with the command to reach it, for example "Work on servera: ssh opsadmin@servera".
- The [LAB:...] prompt marker also shows on the server while a lab runs there.
- Lab scripts get the task user as LAB_USER (student on the workstation, opsadmin on a server), and task.txt shows it with the {{LAB_USER}} placeholder.
- A Target column in the lab catalog.
- lib/packages.sh, the shared package cleanup. pkg_snapshot records the package set at a lab's first start and pkg_restore puts it back at reset; pkg_snapshot_node and pkg_restore_node do the same on the nodes of the multi-node labs.
- labctl reset removes every package, repo key, module stream file and repo file that a lab added since its first start, and reinstalls packages that went missing. It never downgrades, so an upgrade pulled in during the lab stays.
- labctl reset removes the system users and groups that packages created during the lab, when they own no files, together with such a user's empty mail spool.
- scripts/test-lab.sh checks on every machine of a lab that the package set and the system users and groups after reset match those before start.
- check-labs.sh requires every lab that installs packages to use lib/packages.sh, and every such lab does.
- Known issues files for logging-01 (journalctl on Rocky 8), clustering-02 (fence_virsh has no hypervisor to reach) and packages-04 (EPEL mirror 404s).
- labctl start refuses to start a lab while another one is active and tells the student to run sudo labctl reset <active lab> first. Before, it overwrote the marker and the first lab was never cleaned up. Starting the active lab again still works.
- labctl records where it started the active lab in /opt/linux-labs/.current_target. A lab that 1.1.0 started and that is still active after the upgrade is recognised by the missing record: labctl task and labctl grade say it was started with an older version of linux-labs, and sudo labctl reset runs its cleanup on the workstation, where 1.1.0 ran it, and on servera.
- labctl check, a read-only check of the classroom environment: the configuration file and the server addresses, the SSH key, the sudoers rule for labctl, and on servera (and serverb and serverc when multi-node labs are on) the SSH login without a password, passwordless sudo and the release. It warns when servera has fewer than two free NICs or cannot reach its package repositories. Each FAIL line comes with a fix line, and the command exits 1 when a required check fails.

### Changed
- Upgrading from 1.1.0: reset active labs before the upgrade. 1.1.0 ran every lab on the workstation; a lab still active after the upgrade must be reset with 2.0.0, which cleans it up on the workstation and on servera.
- All 55 labs converted to framework 2.0 and reviewed one by one. Setup is silent, cleanup undoes both setup and the student's solution, and solution.md follows a common format.
- labctl grade now re-runs itself through sudo for the student, so graders run as root and can read root-only state.
- Config lookup in labctl follows SUDO_USER, so sudo labctl reads the config the student saved with labctl configure.
- load-config.sh works under set -euo pipefail, and run_on_node uses BatchMode and a connect timeout, so a missing SSH key fails at once instead of hanging on a prompt.
- Documentation rewritten into docs/ by audience: student, teacher and lab author. It replaces QUICKSTART, CONFIGURE_SYSTEM and STATIC_IPS_GUIDE, and was checked against the code for the default network, the node address formula and config precedence.
- The framework spec moved from CLAUDE.md to docs/author/framework.md, which CLAUDE.md imports. LAB_IDEAS moved to docs/lab-ideas.md and lists only proposed ideas. README is a short entry point.
- Repository root cleaned: install.sh and the RPM signing key moved to pages/.
- CI runs shellcheck from the same docker image as local runs (SHELLCHECK=docker). The apt version on the runner reported SC2015 on chains that the current release accepts.
- The labctl man page updated for the new commands.
- Every single-node lab now runs on servera, where the student works as opsadmin with full sudo. On the workstation the student has sudo only for labctl. The workstation target stays valid for labs that need no root, and no lab uses it today.
- The default SSH_USER in labctl, load-config.sh and the config template is opsadmin.
- scripts/test-lab.sh runs solve.sh, the reboot and the leftover checks on the lab's target machine.
- storage-01 and systemd-04 reboot servera, and their tasks say that the SSH connection closes during the reboot and is opened again afterwards.
- Solutions install a package only when it is missing, so they never upgrade one that is already there.
- The MySQL and PostgreSQL labs keep a server that existed before the lab. mysql-01 and postgres-01 set it aside and put it back at reset, and the other labs restore its accounts, configuration and service state.
- webserver-01 to webserver-03 start without httpd again, so the first task is to install it, and reset brings back an httpd that was there before together with its configuration.
- The load balancing and clustering labs remove the packages the student is to install from the nodes at setup, and reset puts back what each node had before.
- firewall-02 creates its own NetworkManager connection, fwlab, on the free interface, and the student assigns the interface to the zone on that connection.
- clustering-02 and clustering-03 build the clustering-01 cluster when it is missing, so each one runs on its own.
- clustering-03 no longer grades STONITH. fence_virsh cannot reach a hypervisor in the classroom, and a cluster with fencing on and no working fence device does not run its resource.
- The replication tasks say what reset does to the database servers on the nodes.

### Fixed
- Every lab was runtime-tested on Rocky Linux 8.10 and 9.8. On Rocky 9, users-02 could not verify passwords hashed with a rounds setting; its grader now uses the system crypt().
- Graders that could never pass, and graders that passed without checking anything.
- Solutions that did not satisfy their own task text.
- Cleanups that destroyed data or left the VM in a changed state.
- Network labs that modified the interface used for the SSH session.
- Differences between Rocky Linux 8 and 9 that broke setup, grading or the solution.
- labctl configure no longer reports success for a config write that failed.
- labctl reset of one lab removed the active-lab marker of another lab that was still active, on the workstation and on servera, and also that lab's working copy on servera.
- The labctl configure wizard showed a wrong example network and node address; it now matches the default 172.25.250.0/24 and node 1 at .10.
- Lab scripts lost their exec bit in the copy labctl makes on a server, so a setup that runs its own cleanup.sh failed with Permission denied.
- check-labs.sh failed the package criterion in CI with a broken pipe from GNU sed, while BSD sed on macOS stayed silent.
- The network labs wrote NetworkManager's in-memory "Wired connection" profiles to disk. They now turn autoconnect off in memory only and restore exactly those profiles at reset.
- firewall-02 sometimes graded a correct solution FAIL, because NetworkManager kept reactivating the free interface and each activation reset its zone.
- networking-03 could pick an interface with an address as a bond port, and left the bonding module loaded.
- mysql-02 and mysql-03 broke on a server with a /root/.my.cnf, because its password overrode the lab password. Lab logins now pass --no-defaults.
- Setup printed to stderr before the task header: initdb and psql notices in postgres-02 and postgres-03, and "Importing GPG key" from dnf in selinux-03, scheduling-01, scheduling-03 and logging-02. Multi-node setups are silent on success too.
- The multi-node node scripts ran commands as opsadmin without sudo; they now use sudo -n.
- Multi-node cleanups removed httpd and other services that were on the nodes before the lab. Setup now records each node's state and cleanup restores it.
- Lab fixes found by runtime tests on Rocky 8.7: users-02 (chage output padded with tabs), logging-01 (journalctl 239 output), selinux-01 (PASS right after reset), webserver-02 (httpd -S with one virtual host), webserver-03 (syntax check before the certificate existed), postgres-01 (process name postmaster), replication-01 and replication-03 (SHOW REPLICA STATUS read without field names), lb-02 (a backend marked down skewed the balancing check) and clustering-02 (fence-agents-virsh missing from the solution).
- clustering-01 removes stale cluster configuration that leaked into the new cluster.
- users-02 restores /etc/login.defs exactly at reset, and selinux-02 restores the httpd service state it found.
- The named, mysql, apache, nginx and cluster accounts stayed after reset; the labs now remove the data those accounts own before the package restore.

### Removed
- test_static_ips.sh, a manual smoke test that only ran from a checkout at /root/linux-labs.
- QUICKSTART.md, CONFIGURE_SYSTEM.md, STATIC_IPS_GUIDE.md and LAB_IDEAS.md from the repository root.
- The mixed legacy lab format. Every lab uses framework 2.0.

## 1.1.0 (2026-10-01)

First public release.

### Added
- GitHub Actions pipeline that builds the RPM on every push and publishes a release on a version tag.
- Signed RPM and a dnf repository on GitHub Pages, with the public key published next to it.
- curl installer (install.sh) that sets up the repository and installs linux-labs.
- Smoke tests of the built RPM on Rocky Linux 8 and 9.
- Labs files-04, packages-04 and packages-05.
- Multi-node labs: replication-01 to 03, lb-01 to 03 and a 3-node Pacemaker series, clustering-01 to 03, with the interactive labctl configure command and RH classroom defaults (network 172.25.250.0/24, gateway 172.25.250.254).

### Changed
- Default gateway aligned to 172.25.250.254 in labctl, the library and the docs.
- files-02 uses the apache user instead of www-data.

### Fixed
- labctl installed as 0755 instead of setuid 4755. The kernel ignores setuid on scripts and sudo already grants root.
- Sudoers rule marked config(noreplace) and validated with visudo during the build.
- Duplicate entries in the spec file list.
- Grading scripts incremented counters with post-increment, so a passing check also ran the failure branch.
- Cleanup scripts of the clustering labs, and cleanup output that was too verbose.

## 1.0 (2026-01-23)

Initial release, an RPM built by hand on a local machine.

### Added
- The first lab set (firewall, logging, networking, packages, scheduling, SELinux, storage, systemd, users, webserver, MySQL, PostgreSQL and DNS), run with labctl start, grade, reset, list and solution.
- A basic man page for labctl.
